CHAPTER.VERS:
And I said, Hear, I pray you

          {+}
        , you

          {+}
         heads of Jacob, and rulers of the house of Israel: is it not for you

          {+}
         to know justice?

You

          {+}
         who hate the good, and love the evil; who pluck off their skin from off them, and their flesh from off their bones;

Therefore it will be night to you

          {+}
        , that you

          {+}
         will have no vision; and it will be dark to you

          {+}
        , that you

          {+}
         will not have fortune-telling; and the sun will go down on the prophets, and the day will be black over them.

Hear this, I pray you

          {+}
        , you

          {+}
         heads of the house of Jacob, and rulers of the house of Israel, who are disgusted by justice, and pervert all equity.

Therefore will Zion for your

          {+}
         sake be plowed as a field, and Jerusalem will become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of a forest.
